# Auth / private pages — never cache, block indexing
# /publish is an INDEXABLE conversion landing page (changed 2026-09-16, §AF).
# It has a bespoke SEO treatment — dedicated title/description/H1 and a
# `seoPrerender` entry (apps/api/src/lib/seoPrerender.ts:704) rendering 82 KB of
# real content, verified live — and 41 internal links point at it. It was
# nevertheless BOTH Disallowed in robots.txt AND noindexed here, so all that
# link equity was thrown away and the page could never rank for its target
# query ("publicar viaje a concierto"). The form below the fold needs auth, but
# the page itself is public marketing content, exactly like /como-funciona.
# No Cache-Control: no-store either — that was only needed for authed content.

/profile
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/mis-viajes
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/favoritos
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/login
